---
source: crates/eval/src/tests/caches.rs
expression: "err(&[(\"system.toml\",\n\"[system]\\nhostname = \\\"box\\\"\\n\\n[caches.none]\\n\\n[caches.bad]\\nurl = 3\\n\\n\\\n             [caches.typo]\\nurl = \\\"/c\\\"\\nkey = []\\n\\n[caches.short]\\nurl = \\\"/c\\\"\\n\\\n             keys = [\\\"home:abc\\\"]\\n\\n[caches.home]\\nurl = \\\"/c\\\"\\n\",),\n(\"services/other.toml\", \"[caches.home]\\nurl = \\\"/elsewhere\\\"\\n\"),\n(\"services/flat.toml\", \"caches = \\\"/c\\\"\\n\"),])"
---
error: a cache's `url` is a string, found integer
 --> system.toml:7:7
  |
7 | url = 3
  |       ^ expected a directory or an `https://` URL

error: cache `none` has no `url`
 --> system.toml:4:1
  |
4 | [caches.none]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `url = "..."`

error: a cache key is `name:` and 64 hex digits
  --> system.toml:15:9
   |
15 | keys = ["home:abc"]
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^ not a key
   = help: `wrath cache key` prints a key to paste here

error: unexpected `key` in a cache
  --> system.toml:11:1
   |
11 | key = []
   | ^^^ only `url` and `keys` belong here

error: `caches` is a table of caches by name
 --> services/flat.toml:1:10
  |
1 | caches = "/c"
  |          ^^^^ expected `[caches.NAME]`
  = help: for example `[caches.home]` with `url = "https://..."`

error: cache `home` is defined twice, differently
  --> system.toml:17:1
   |
17 | [caches.home]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ once here
  --> services/other.toml:1:1
   |
 1 | [caches.home]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ and again here
